sequenceDiagram
    participant H as Host (Rust)
    participant S as Signaling (Go)
    participant V as Viewer (browser)

    H->>S: WebSocket connect (role=host, token)
    S->>H: config (STUN and TURN servers,<br/>short-lived TURN credentials)
    V->>S: WebSocket connect (role=viewer, token)
    S->>V: config (same, freshly minted)
    S->>H: viewer-joined
    H->>H: new peer connection, "input" data channel,<br/>create offer n, gather ICE candidates
    H->>S: offer (SDP with candidates, session n)
    S->>V: offer
    V->>V: new peer connection, create answer,<br/>gather candidates (at most 3 s)
    V->>V: refuse if the host key differs from the saved one,<br/>otherwise show the pairing code
    V->>S: answer (SDP with candidates, session n)
    S->>H: answer
    H->>H: viewer key paired? If not, print the same code<br/>and wait for y on the terminal before applying the answer
    H-->>V: ICE connectivity checks (direct UDP,<br/>or relayed through coturn if blocked)
    H-->>V: DTLS handshake, then encrypted H.264 over SRTP
    V-->>H: input data channel opens (viewer to host messages)
    Note over H,V: A page reload reconnects the viewer: the server sends<br/>viewer-joined again and the host starts session n+1
